Funis
=====

Funis is a fork of mold, https://github.com/rui314/mold, created by Rui Ueyama
and distributed under the MIT licence (see LICENSE). The fork was started on
2026-10-15 from mold 3.0.0 at commit c522789 ("Mark the Mach-O build ID as a
version-3 UUID").

All code present at that commit is the work of mold's authors. The Funis
changes are recorded in this repository's git history on the `funis` branch;
the `upstream` remote points at mold.

The external crate `mold-mimalloc` is a dependency published by the mold
project and is used under its own licence.

Location and what was kept
--------------------------

Since 2026-10-15 Funis is a component of the Codira workspace. It is a
snapshot of the `funis` branch of the standalone repository at the time (mold
3.0.0 at commit c522789, plus the Funis commits 715b339, the rename, and
46f3a3a, the thread pool sized to the input), split into Cargo crates under
`crates/`:

    funis              the command line (`funis`, `ld64.funis`) and the library API
    funis_common       code the two linkers share
    funis_elf          the generic ELF linker
    funis_macho        the generic Mach-O linker
    funis_elf_x86_64, funis_elf_arm64, funis_elf_riscv64
                       the ELF linker instantiated for Codira's ELF targets
    funis_macho_arm64, funis_macho_x86_64
                       the Mach-O linker instantiated for Codira's Mach-O targets
    funis_tests        the harness that runs the shell tests (see tests/)

The standalone repository (C:/Users/RAIDER/Documents/GitHub/funis, remote
`upstream` = mold) kept the history. Compared with mold, this tree does not
build, test or ship the other ELF targets: i386, arm32 and arm32be, arm64be,
riscv32, riscv32be and riscv64be, ppc32, ppc64v1 and ppc64v2, s390x, sparc64,
m68k, sh4 and sh4be, loongarch32 and loongarch64. Their instantiation crates
(`arch/elf-*`) were left out, and so were the `dist.sh` and `install-funis.sh`
release scripts. The generic `funis_elf` crate still contains the target
descriptions of those architectures (`funis_elf/arch/*.rs`), untouched so that
mold's changes keep applying cleanly, but nothing instantiates them; asking
for one of them reports "unsupported target". To bring one back, copy its
`arch/elf-<name>` crate from the standalone repository, add it to the
workspace, and add a feature and a table entry in `crates/funis`.

The shell tests of mold (`tests/elf/*.sh`, `tests/macho/*.sh`) are kept under
`crates/funis/tests/`. They need a Unix host with a C compiler (macOS for the
Mach-O ones) and are skipped elsewhere, so `cargo test --workspace` on Windows
does not run them.

Codira is licensed under Apache-2.0; Funis keeps mold's MIT licence, in
`crates/funis/LICENSE-MIT`, and every Funis crate declares `license = "MIT"`.
